===Pronunciation===
{{IPA|[ˈbrɛnːɪvʊin]}}
===Etymology===
Composition of ''[[brenna]]'' (to burn) and ''[[vín]]'' (wine), analogous to Danish ''[[brændevin]]'' from German ''[[Branntwein]]'' ([[brandy]]).
